    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The technical picture for AMZN remains constructive \u2014 price sits above all three key moving averages (10 EMA $168.98, 50 SMA $156.41, 200 SMA $137.23) with a bullish stack and exceptional FY2023 operating cash flow of $84.95B. However, early momentum fatigue signals (MACD histogram turned negative at -0.04, RSI cooling from 73.78 to 60.56, below-average relative volume of 0.91) and the genuine absence of income statement data, macro context, and sentiment data prevent the conviction needed for a BUY. The risk/reward is roughly balanced (+5.3% to Bollinger upper band vs -7.7% to 50 SMA), and the trend is clearly up with a shallow 2.83% pullback, so a SELL is not warranted. Maintaining current positioning while awaiting either a confirmed breakout above $174.45 on strong volume or a pullback to the 50 SMA for a better entry is the prudent stance.\n\n**Entry Price**: 169.51\n\n**Stop Loss**: 156.41\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current position; if adding on confirmed breakout above $174.45, size at 50-60% of maximum intended allocation given elevated realized volatility (35.33% annualized) and ATR of $3.81\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
